{{smaller block|Thei sporered theire horse over the brigge at a ''brunt.''
{{right|''Merlin'', ii. 282.}}
I must resolve to stand to the hazard of all ''brunts'' now.
{{right|''Ford'', Love’s Sacrifice, v. 2.}}
It is instantly and irrecoverably scattered by our first ''brunt'' with some real affair of common life. ''Is. Taylor.''}}
